 ## Schema compilation and caching

-- A static `ToolDefinition` has its `inputSchema` compiled once at `register` time, so a schema that is not valid JSON Schema throws synchronously from `register` with an error message naming the offending tool ([validated by: throws at register time naming the tool when a static inputSchema cannot be compiled](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L94), [validated by: throws synchronously naming the tool when registering an invalid static inputSchema](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L4)).
-- A static tool's `inputSchema` is compiled at `register` time and reused on every `execute` call without re-reading or re-compiling `definition.inputSchema` ([validated by: reuses the static validator across repeated execute calls without re-reading inputSchema](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L13)).
